    },
    {
      "id": "M1",
      "kind": "mixed",
      "parents": [
        "K0023",
        "K0031",
        "K0043"
      ],
      "text": "When both the architecture and the optimizer settings differ, the candidate whose cumulative step size is at least 2x larger usually wins regardless of architecture (adaptive optimizers; see the step-size notes for the language-model exception at lr 3e-3). Architecture notes decide mainly when the step sizes are within 2x of each other.",
      "inject_same": [],
      "rules": [
