        "R2 usage limit",
        "R5 (v2 descriptive)"
      ],
      "text": "At comparable parameter counts (within 2x), an MLP that trades width for depth wins when the networks have residual connections or LayerNorm: the deeper, narrower one is better. For plain MLPs with neither residual connections nor LayerNorm the shallower, wider one is better.",
      "inject_same": [],
      "rules": [
